## The six terms

| Term | Agreed position | Default if unstated |
|---|---|---|
| **Residency** — which tenant holds captured evidence | {{RESIDENCY}} | Client tenant |
| **Retention** — how long, and what happens at close | | Defined period, deletion at close |
| **Redaction** — what is stripped before it leaves the client environment | | Redact by default |
| **Access** — who on the HGS side may read it | | Named engagement team only |
| **Deletion** — mechanism, who confirms, evidence of deletion | | Documented, confirmed in writing |
| **Onward use** — may a generalised pattern reach the practice asset library | | Yes, after generalisation strips all identifying material |

Ask for onward use at the start, while goodwill is high and the request is abstract. It is the term teams forget to ask for and then need.

## Monitoring constraint

**Desktop task mining and session replay are employee monitoring, whatever the vendor's deck calls them.** In EU works-council jurisdictions and unionised environments they require **consultation, not notice** — a process with a counterparty who can say no, taking weeks.

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Jurisdiction(s) | |
| Labour representation | {{LABOUR}} |
| Consultation required | |
| Consultation status | |
| Techniques in scope | |
| Always-on instrumentation proposed | |

**Where there is doubt, prefer consented, time-boxed shadowing.** It produces better material anyway: an operator who agreed to be there will show you the exception.

